# Redoubt session-cleanup.patch  (Android, LW-M7-37)
#
# 157 rebase (Firefox 157.0, was 153.4.0esr). What moved upstream:
#   - netwerk/cookie: 157 buffers cookie database writes in CookieDBWriteQueue
#     (coalesced, flushed on a timer). ReadCleanupScopes and DeleteCleanupScopes
#     now FlushNow() the queue first; the connection runs async statements in
#     order, so the read sees every earlier change and an insertion queued
#     before the lease cannot re-create a row after the cleanup DELETE.
#   - 157 dropped CookiePersistentStorage's RemoveCookiesWithOriginAttributes /
#     RemoveCookiesFromExactHost overrides and their mozStorageTransaction; the
#     base-class removals now go through the write queue. There is no
#     caller-owned SQL transaction left for the cleanup statement to join, so
#     the 153 guards on those two overrides are gone with them.
#     RunInTransaction is still a caller-owned batch scope: it keeps the guard
#     (refused while a lease is held; no lease may begin inside it).
#   - nsFrameLoader.h: mRemoteType is a RemoteType now (context only).
#   - include lists in CookieService.cpp, CookieStorage.cpp,
#     CookiePersistentStorage.{h,cpp} were re-sorted upstream.
#
